 "notes": "Old k51 (72 models) redistributed by style: icons became archetypes (Dom Pérignon, Cristal, Krug, Comtes de Champagne, La Grande Dame, Belle Époque, Grand Siècle, Sir Winston Churchill, Dom Ruinart, Cuvée Louise, Celebris, Femme de Champagne, R.D., VVF, Clos du Mesnil, Yellow Label, Brut Impérial, Special Cuvée, LP La Cuvée/Heritage); the rest kept as flat m in the kind that fits their style. Dropped as duplicates: 'Lanson Noble Brut' (= Noble Cuvée), 'Rare' by Piper-Heidsieck and 'Rare Champagne Brut' (Rare is now its own label; kept 'Rare Millésime Brut' and 'Rare Rose'), 'Rare Champagne Rare Magnum' (bottle size, not a cuvée), 'Ruinart Rose Brut' and 'Grand Millésime' (now archetypes). Grand Siècle has no own page fetched; sourced to the Champagne article listing it as a prestige cuvée. Grande Marque status left out (no fetched source). No brand entries for old-data makers without a fetched page (Abelé, Ayala, Deutz, Henriot, Drappier, Jacquesson, Nicolas Feuillatte etc.). No traditions: Champagne production is covered by producer and dosage types, not artisan craft."
